\chapter{Lessons and the page}

The page is React and Tailwind. It holds the lesson text and the recognised name,
and it does not hold any per-frame state. The scene, with the physics world, the
renderer and the rope tube, lives in one component, which creates them when it
mounts and disposes of them when it unmounts.

\section{Lesson record}

A lesson is data. It names the knot, the stage that teaches it, its web sources,
the invariants a recogniser must match, and the prompt the player reads. Stage
one has one record, the overhand knot, so the page has something to show. The
guided, sandbox and quiz modes arrive in later stages and read the same records.

The source is the Knot Atlas entry for 3\textsubscript{1}, which the research
chapter records as confirmed. The determinant is three, as the topology chapter
computes.

@d Lessons: record and stub @{
export interface Invariants {
  determinant: number;
}

export interface LessonRecord {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  stage: number;
  sources: readonly string[];
  invariants: Invariants;
  prompt: string;
}

export const STAGE_ONE_LESSONS: readonly LessonRecord[] = [
  {
    id: 'overhand',
    name: 'Overhand knot',
    stage: 1,
    sources: ['https://katlas.org/wiki/3_1'],
    invariants: { determinant: 3 },
    prompt: 'Tie an overhand knot in the rope. The recogniser names it when it is tied.',
  },
];
@}

\section{Anchor}

The bar is the one anchor in stage one. It is scene data: a box with a centre and
half sizes. The rope model receives it as a plain shape, and the renderer draws
it as a mesh. Neither owns it. The bar lies along the depth axis, so a rope that
is dragged across it in the view can drape over it, and the rope cannot pass
through it.

@d Anchors: bar @{
import type { Box } from '../rope/snapshot';

export const BAR: Box = {
  center: { x: 0.6, y: 0.2, z: 0 },
  half: { x: 0.02, y: 0.02, z: 0.4 },
};
@}

\section{Rope stage}

The stage component owns the whole scene. Three effects keep it honest.

The physics loop runs only while the rope moves. When the fastest link is slower
than the settle speed for thirty frames, the loop stops, and a pointer event
starts it again. That is render on demand, as the architecture chapter asks.

Recognition runs at most four times a second while the rope moves, and once when
it settles. It sets state only when the name changes, so React re-renders on a
change of result, never on each frame.

Pointer input moves the grab point in the plane facing the viewer. The wheel
moves it in depth, because a knot needs depth, and a drag in the plane alone
produces none.

@d UI: rope stage @{
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { RopeTube } from '../render/ropeTube';
import { BAR } from '../anchors/bar';
import { LINK_COUNT, LINK_RADIUS, createRope, initPhysics, type Rope } from '../rope/rope';
import { recognise } from '../topology/recogniser';

const TOP = { x: 0, y: 1.2, z: 0 };
const SETTLE_SPEED = 0.01;
const SETTLE_FRAMES = 30;
const RECOGNISE_EVERY_MS = 250;
const DEPTH_STEP = 0.002;

export function RopeStage() {
  const hostRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const [name, setName] = useState<string | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const host = hostRef.current;
    if (!host) return;

    let disposed = false;
    let frame = 0;
    let running = false;
    let rope: Rope | null = null;
    let tube: RopeTube | null = null;
    let renderer: THREE.WebGLRenderer | null = null;
    let barGeometry: THREE.BoxGeometry | null = null;
    let barMaterial: THREE.MeshStandardMaterial | null = null;
    let still = 0;
    let lastRecognised = 0;
    let grabZ = 0;
    let cleanup = () => {};
    const target = { x: TOP.x, y: TOP.y, z: TOP.z };

    const raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();
    const pointer = new THREE.Vector2();
    const plane = new THREE.Plane();
    const hit = new THREE.Vector3();
    let dragging = false;

    initPhysics().then(() => {
      if (disposed) return;

      rope = createRope(TOP, [BAR]);
      tube = new RopeTube(LINK_COUNT, LINK_RADIUS);

      const scene = new THREE.Scene();
      scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x0f172a);
      scene.add(tube.mesh);
      scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.6));
      const light = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1.2);
      light.position.set(1, 2, 3);
      scene.add(light);

      barGeometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(BAR.half.x * 2, BAR.half.y * 2, BAR.half.z * 2);
      barMaterial = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x64748b });
      const barMesh = new THREE.Mesh(barGeometry, barMaterial);
      barMesh.position.set(BAR.center.x, BAR.center.y, BAR.center.z);
      scene.add(barMesh);

      const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(40, host.clientWidth / host.clientHeight, 0.01, 100);
      camera.position.set(0, 0.2, 4);
      camera.lookAt(0, 0.2, 0);

      renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });
      renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));
      renderer.setSize(host.clientWidth, host.clientHeight);
      host.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

      const canvas = renderer.domElement;
      const draw = renderer;
      const world = rope;
      const strip = tube;

      const animate = () => {
        const fastest = world.step();
        const snapshot = world.snapshot();
        strip.update(snapshot);
        draw.render(scene, camera);

        still = fastest < SETTLE_SPEED ? still + 1 : 0;
        const now = performance.now();
        if (still === SETTLE_FRAMES || (still === 0 && now - lastRecognised > RECOGNISE_EVERY_MS)) {
          lastRecognised = now;
          setName(recognise(snapshot).name);
        }
        if (still < SETTLE_FRAMES) {
          frame = requestAnimationFrame(animate);
        } else {
          running = false;
        }
      };

      const wake = () => {
        still = 0;
        if (!running) {
          running = true;
          frame = requestAnimationFrame(animate);
        }
      };

      const moveGrab = (event: PointerEvent) => {
        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
        pointer.set(
          ((event.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1,
          -((event.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1,
        );
        raycaster.setFromCamera(pointer, camera);
        plane.set(new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 1), -grabZ);
        if (raycaster.ray.intersectPlane(plane, hit)) {
          target.x = hit.x;
          target.y = hit.y;
          target.z = grabZ;
          world.grab(target);
          wake();
        }
      };

      const onDown = (event: PointerEvent) => {
        dragging = true;
        canvas.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
        moveGrab(event);
      };
      const onMove = (event: PointerEvent) => {
        if (dragging) moveGrab(event);
      };
      const onUp = () => {
        dragging = false;
      };
      const onWheel = (event: WheelEvent) => {
        grabZ = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, grabZ - event.deltaY * DEPTH_STEP));
        target.z = grabZ;
        world.grab(target);
        wake();
      };
      const onResize = () => {
        camera.aspect = host.clientWidth / host.clientHeight;
        camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
        draw.setSize(host.clientWidth, host.clientHeight);
      };

      canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', onDown);
      canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', onMove);
      canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', onUp);
      canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', onUp);
      canvas.addEventListener('wheel', onWheel);
      window.addEventListener('resize', onResize);

      cleanup = () => {
        canvas.removeEventListener('pointerdown', onDown);
        canvas.removeEventListener('pointermove', onMove);
        canvas.removeEventListener('pointerup', onUp);
        canvas.removeEventListener('pointercancel', onUp);
        canvas.removeEventListener('wheel', onWheel);
        window.removeEventListener('resize', onResize);
      };

      wake();
    });

    return () => {
      disposed = true;
      cancelAnimationFrame(frame);
      cleanup();
      rope?.dispose();
      tube?.dispose();
      barGeometry?.dispose();
      barMaterial?.dispose();
      if (renderer) {
        renderer.dispose();
        renderer.domElement.remove();
      }
    };
  }, []);

  return (
    <div className="relative h-full w-full">
      <div ref={hostRef} className="absolute inset-0" />
      <p className="pointer-events-none absolute bottom-3 left-3 rounded bg-slate-900/80 px-2 py-1 text-sm text-slate-200">
        Recognised: {name ?? 'nothing yet'}
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
@}

\section{Application}

The application is one screen: the lesson's name and prompt at the top, the rope
stage filling the rest. The stage is the only part with per-frame work.

@d UI: application @{
import { STAGE_ONE_LESSONS } from './lessons/record';
import { RopeStage } from './ui/RopeStage';

export function App() {
  const lesson = STAGE_ONE_LESSONS[0];
  return (
    <main className="flex h-full flex-col bg-slate-950 text-slate-100">
      <header className="border-b border-slate-800 px-4 py-3">
        <h1 className="text-lg font-semibold">Roppi</h1>
        <p className="text-sm text-slate-400">
          {lesson.name}. {lesson.prompt}
        </p>
      </header>
      <section className="relative min-h-0 flex-1">
        <RopeStage />
      </section>
    </main>
  );
}
@}
